      "defect": "ill-formed",
      "evidence": "The item calls constituent circles “1-cells.” But def-cell-attachment-by-a-characteristic-map defines an open 1-cell as the image of the interior of D^1, hence an open interval; a constituent circle is S^1 and includes the common vertex. Thus the proposed objects do not literally form the claimed cell structure. The intended conclusion remains correct when the punctured circles are the open cells and the circles are their closures.",
